========================================================================
SOURCE REVIEW (7.1 — no product edit)
========================================================================

`ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret_guard.oo` (200 lines, under monofile ratchet):

```
pub fn c_guard_scan_idents(env, sink, args)
  linear walk of C arg text
  skip "..." with \\ escapes (in_str)
  skip // line comments and /* */ block comments (C-arg defense)
  ident = [_A-Za-z][_A-Za-z0-9]*
  name = str_slice(args, start, i)   // ONE slice per span
  c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved(env, sink, name)
```

`c_secret_emit_guard`:
- callee resolved: `sink = c_secret_resolve_alias(env, t)` (CRIT 2.4)
- named sealed sinks then `c_guard_scan_idents(env, sink, args)` including
  `println` / `eprintln` / `print_err` / `log` / `fprintf` / `syslog`

Check dual (`c_emit_secret.oo` `check_secret_println_sinks`): token IDENT
walk of println/eprintln args after the same alias resolve. Strings are
`STRING` tokens (not `IDENT`). Lexer drops `//` comments before the walk.

Honest 7.1 reading vs ticket wording:
- Ticket says “stack buffer.” `.oo` has **no** stack `char buf[N]`.
- Alpha close = **slice, not quadratic concat**. That land is live.

7.10 still `name = name + c` in `c_parse_secret_env` — **not** 7.1.

