========================================================================
RESIDUALS (honest, out of 7.1 gate)
========================================================================

1. **7.10 still OPEN** — `c_parse_secret_env` accumulates `name = name + c`.
   Do not close 7.10 on this peer.
2. **`/* */` source comments** — not product lex at check. Emit-time
   `c_guard_scan_idents` skips C `/* */` in **lowered arg text** (defense
   for C), which is a different layer. SECRET_TAINT §5 already: “Not full
   block-comment / raw-string / interpolation `${}` hardening.”
3. **Check cache poison** — `check_mod.oo` `run_check_path` hits
   `.ooda-cache/check/t_<content_hash>` and prints `OK` without re-running
   `check_secret_println_sinks`. Hash is source-only, not compiler-id.
   First dirty-cwd `check` of `secret_sink_fail.oo` returned OK; clean-cwd
   re-prove refused. **Process residual** for dual-path audits. Emit-c is
   the honest refuse rail.
4. **7.2** (`c_sys_exec_last_arg` slice) is adjacent, not this close.
5. Full IFC / `${}` interp / higher-order beyond `__alias__` depth 16 —
   residual (SECRET_TAINT).

